CE14-reagent-name-blood-animal = Animal blood
CE14-reagent-desc-blood-animal = The life energy of a living unintelligent being.

CE14-reagent-name-blood-vampire = Vampire blood
CE14-reagent-desc-blood-vampire = The life energy of a powerful blood-vampire.

CE14-reagent-name-blood = Blood
CE14-reagent-desc-blood = The life energy of a living warm-blooded creatures.

CE14-reagent-name-blood-tiefling = Tiefling blood
CE14-reagent-desc-blood-tiefling = The life energy of a fire-blooded creature.

CE14-reagent-name-blood-elf = Elf blood
CE14-reagent-desc-blood-elf = The life energy of a magical creature.

CE14-reagent-name-blood-goblin = Goblin blood
CE14-reagent-desc-blood-goblin = The life energy of green-skinned creatures.

CE14-reagent-name-blood-monster = Monster blood
CE14-reagent-desc-blood-monster = The life energy of various monsters.

CE14-reagent-name-bloodflowersap = Bloodrose nectar
CE14-reagent-desc-bloodflowersap = The nectar of the bloody flowers that grow in former battlefields. When properly mixed with blood, it can produce interesting results.

CE14-reagent-name-yellow-dayflin-pulp = Yellow dayfline pulp
CE14-reagent-desc-yellow-dayflin-pulp = Crushed flowers of sunny dayflines.

CE14-reagent-name-air-lily-juice = Air lily juice
CE14-reagent-desc-air-lily-juice = The juice of flowers growing on water. Possesses healing air properties.

CE14-reagent-name-agaric-shroom = Fly agaric juice
CE14-reagent-desc-agaric-shroom = It is this juice that the fly mushrooms owe their poisonousness to. Consumption causes severe ailments and hallucinations, but experienced alchemists can find other uses for these mushrooms.

CE14-reagent-name-blue-amanita = Blue amanita
CE14-reagent-desc-blue-amanita = A sky blue flower known for its medicinal and magical properties.

CE14-reagent-name-lumi-shroom = Lumishroom sap
CE14-reagent-desc-lumi-shroom = A faintly shimmering slurry extracted from lumigrib. Often used by alchemists as a means of concentrating solutions.

CE14-reagent-name-wild-sage-sap = Wild sage juice
CE14-reagent-desc-wild-sage-sap = Juice of a ubiquitous medicinal plant, not bad at healing physical injuries, and inducing coughing.

CE14-reagent-name-sleepy-poison = Whistler poison
CE14-reagent-desc-sleepy-poison = A poison secreted by dangerous magical monsters to quickly put their victim to sleep.

CE14-reagent-name-whistler-poison = Whistler poison
CE14-reagent-desc-whistler-poison = A poison secreted by a dangerous magical monster to quickly put its victim to sleep.

CE14-reagent-name-grounded-quartz = Ground quartz
CE14-reagent-desc-grounded-quartz = A powder obtained from grinding quartz fragments. It has weak cleaning properties.

CE14-reagent-name-chromium-slime = Chromium slime
CE14-reagent-desc-chromium-slime = A rare substance found in water streams, it has unique properties that allow it to invert the effects of reagents, but can completely ruin a potion if dosed incorrectly.

CE14-reagent-name-silver-needle = Silver needle berries
CE14-reagent-desc-silver-needle = The berries of a plant that survives the harshest frosts. The juice of these berries slows down metabolism and can treat frostbite.